    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "COMING\nUNEQUALLED COMFORT AND SPEED\nIN THE SPACIOUS, SMOOTH-RIDING\nBOEING\nStrate iver\nON KEY ROUTES OF\nNORTHWEST\nAIRLINES",
      "SEPARATE, LARGE DRESS-\nING ROOMS FOR MEN\nAND WOMEN\nSECTION OF MAIN CABIN\nSHOWING DAY SEAT\nARRANGEMENT\nNIGHT BERTH ARRANGE-\nMENT.\nNUMBER\nOF\nBERTHS IS\nVARIABLE\nROOMY CONTROL\nCABIN FOR FLIGHT\nCREW\nSTAIRWAY TO\nLOWER-DECK\nLOUNGE\nMAIN\nLOADING DOOR\nLUXURY\nCOMPARTMENT\nROOMY GALLEY\nFOR HOT MEAL\nSERVICE\nAFT\nLUGGAGE\nCOMPARTMENT\nLOWER-DECK\nLOUNGE SEATING\nSIXTEEN\nFuturndeck\nSTEPS WHICH\nLET DOWN TO\nGROUND LEVEL\nMAIN CARGO HOLD -970\nCUBIC FEET CAPACITY\nSuper Teampers\nINTERIOR ARRANGEMENTS FOR INDIVIDUAL AIR LINES\nMAY VARY FROM THE BASIC INTERIOR SHOWN ABOVE.\nTHE\nBOEING STRATOCRUISER is the first true post-war super transport,\nincorporating not only greater size and comfort, but also, for the first time,\nthe great war-time engineering advancements developed and proved in\nthe Boeing B-29. The cutaway above shows many of its unique features\n- the roomy main upper cabins, distinctive lower deck lounge, ample\ndressing rooms for both men and women, the galley, from which come\ntempting hot meals, and the lower deck forward cargo hold and aft\nluggage compartment accessible in flight.\nCarrying from 55 to 114 passengers, cruising high above surtace\nstorms at well over 300 miles per hour, with a range of more than 4,500\nmiles,\nthe Stratocruiser offers unprecedented standards of performance,\noperating efficiency and reliability.\nYou would expect such an airplane from Boeing, world's leading\nbuilder of four-engine aircraft, pioneer in altitude-conditioning of planes\nfor over-weather flight and creator of such outstanding aircraft as the\nocean-spanning Boeing 314 Flying Boat, Stratoliner, B-17 Flying Fortress\nand B-29 Superfortress.",
      "THE STRATOCRUISER is the first transport with\ntwo passenger decks. An airplane with room\nin which to move about freely, and a lower-\ndeck lounge for your enjoyment.\nSpace and comfort are designed into this\nfirst true super-transport. The main cabin is\n10½ feet wide - considerably wider than a\nrailroad car - has an aisle height of seven feet.\nSeats are roomy, with plenty of leg room for\nstretching out. Berths are 7 inches wider, two\ninches longer than in a sleeping car.\nWhether you're an experienced air traveler\nor making your first flight - you'll find that\nthe Stratocruiser's spaciousness will make your\ntrip still more enjoyable."
    ],
